## Multi-Protocol Conflict Resolution

When multiple protocols trigger simultaneously, E.V.O. applies these rules:

### Priority Hierarchy
```yaml
priority_order:
  1_critical_foundation:
    - meta_surgeon_protocol (if no schema exists)
    - gsc_indexation_protocol (if errors > 100)
  
  2_critical_optimization:
    - gsc_indexation_protocol (if exclusion rate > 30%)
  
  3_high_impact:
    - internal_link_expansion_protocol (if orphaned > 50)
    - keyword_coverage_gap_protocol (if opportunity > 1000 clicks)
  
  4_medium_impact:
    - keyword_coverage_gap_protocol
    - internal_link_expansion_protocol
```

### Resolution Logic
```javascript
function resolveMultipleTriggers(triggers) {
    // Sort by priority and score
    const sorted = triggers.sort((a, b) => {
        // Priority comparison
        const priorityOrder = {
            'critical': 4,
            'high': 3,
            'medium-high': 2,
            'medium': 1
        };
        
        if (priorityOrder[a.priority] !== priorityOrder[b.priority]) {
            return priorityOrder[b.priority] - priorityOrder[a.priority];
        }
        
        // If same priority, sort by score
        return b.score - a.score;
    });
    
    // Special rules
    const topTrigger = sorted[0];
    
    // Rule 1: Always prioritize Meta Surgeon if no schema exists
    const metaTrigger = triggers.find(t => t.cardType === 'meta_surgeon_protocol');
    if (metaTrigger && metaTrigger.score >= 90) {
        return metaTrigger;
    }
    
    // Rule 2: Always prioritize Index Diagnostic if errors > 100
    const indexTrigger = triggers.find(t => t.cardType === 'gsc_indexation_protocol');
    if (indexTrigger && indexTrigger.metrics?.errorPages > 100) {
        return indexTrigger;
    }
    
    // Rule 3: Choose highest priority/score
    return topTrigger;
}
```

### Sequential Card Generation
```javascript
// E.V.O. tracks completed protocols per property
const completedProtocols = await getCompletedProtocols(propertyId);

// Filter out completed protocols from triggers
const availableTriggers = triggers.filter(t => 
    !completedProtocols.includes(t.cardType)
);

// Generate next protocol in sequence
const nextCard = resolveMultipleTriggers(availableTriggers);
```

